// A counterweight's floor is what lies under it now. Let down its rope, it falls to drive the belt; a pillar built
// under it stops it on the pillar's top instead of passing into it (before, it fell through to the floor it had
// when it was hung).
map
################################
################################
#....jjjjjjjjjj*...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j..@............#
#..............*>>>>>>>>>>>....#
################################
end
give Counterweight 1
give WoodPillar 10
place 2 -14 -7 Counterweight
put 100 -14 1 WoodPillar           // a pillar under the weight, two tiles high
put 100 -14 0 WoodPillar
set 101 weight 4
expect 1500 weighty == 7           // resting on the pillar's top (row 9), not down at the floor (row 11)
expect 1500 weights == 1
